WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.834 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yesterday, PETA,

00:00:00.834 --> 00:00:02.669 align:start size:94% position:6%
the People for the
Ethical Treatment of Animals,

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:04.838 size:84% position:42%
tweeted that they think
it's time to get rid of

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
common phrases that
mention cruelty to animals,

00:00:06.806 --> 00:00:11.311
like "kill two birds with one
stone" and "beat a dead horse."

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:13.680 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they went on to say that
using these phrases

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:17.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the same as using
racist or homophobic language.

00:00:17.017 --> 00:00:18.651 size:84% position:42%
Here to talk about that
are two of our writers,

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.187 align:start size:94% position:6%
Jenny Hagel and Amber Ruffin,
in a segment called

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.455 line:92%
"Don't Drag Us Into This."

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:27.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪♪♪

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hey, PETA.
-PETA, What's up?

00:00:29.562 --> 00:00:32.966
-You compared
anti-animal language to racism.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And homophobia.
And as a lesbian...

00:00:35.435 --> 00:00:36.369 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-And a black lady...

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.737 line:92%
-...we just want to say...

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.239 line:92%
-Don't drag us into this.

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:41.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Look, you do good work.
-Great work.

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'd say great work.
-Fantastic work.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But I think people
can see what you're saying

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:49.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
without you comparing
the suffering of animals

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the suffering of
minority groups.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like comparing
apples to oranges

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:56.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Or hamburgers
to voter suppression.

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
-To understand
that something is bad,

00:00:58.925 --> 00:01:01.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
you don't have to compare it
to another bad thing.

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:04.864 size:88% position:44%
Things can be bad all on
their own, like Spanx.

00:01:04.864 --> 00:01:07.067 line:92%
I can tell you how bad they are

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
without comparing them
to World War II.

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:12.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can tell you
why I hate deviled eggs

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.540 line:92%
without talking about polio.

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:16.943 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, I love deviled eggs.
-You're gross.

00:01:16.943 --> 00:01:19.112 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-As gross as slavery.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:22.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
-See? That's what
we don't want you to do.

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:25.518
-Now, Jenny's suffering
isn't the same as my suffering.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:28.588
-And Amber's suffering
isn't the same as my suffering.

00:01:28.588 --> 00:01:30.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
And a duck suffering
sure as [bleep]

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:33.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
isn't the same
as either of them.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.627 line:92%
-Also, let me get this straight.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
Are you saying
when we use an expression

00:01:37.363 --> 00:01:38.398 size:81% position:41% line:92%
that mentions animals,

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.467 align:start size:94% position:6%
you think it hurts
the animal's feelings?

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:43.503
A bull doesn't know you said,
"Grab the bull by the horns."

00:01:43.503 --> 00:01:48.341
Bulls don't even speak English.
-They speak Spanish.

00:01:48.341 --> 00:01:51.644 align:start size:94% position:6%
And to any bulls watching,
I just want to say...

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:56.015 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Speaks Spanish ]

00:01:56.015 --> 00:02:00.453
-And I can see the things
that Jenny goes through

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a gay American,
and they can be valid.

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:06.459
And they can be real without
being tied to my experience.

00:02:06.459 --> 00:02:07.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Same.
-Yeah.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.062 size:81% position:41%
-Amber getting stopped
by security every time

00:02:09.062 --> 00:02:11.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
she goes to JCPenney
isn't the same --

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:13.967 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
You laugh. It happens to her.

00:02:13.967 --> 00:02:15.335 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Big-time.

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:16.236 line:92%
-That's not the same as JCPenney

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:19.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
being able to fire me
in 30 states for being gay.

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Supreme Court
not passing marriage equality

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:23.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
until three years ago
isn't the same

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:26.246
as some white lady
not wanting me to marry her son.

00:02:26.246 --> 00:02:31.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
P.S., I did, and he loves it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.558 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I know you want
animals to be safe.

00:02:38.558 --> 00:02:39.225 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
We all want that.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:42.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'd take a bullet
for this puppy.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:44.998 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I cannot say
the same thing about cats.

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.166 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They are terrible.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:49.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
As terrible as
gay conversion therapy.

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:51.871 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's what we
don't want you to do.

00:02:51.871 --> 00:02:54.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Look, my point is --
if you think it's a good idea

00:02:54.741 --> 00:02:58.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
to compare minority groups to
animals in any way,

00:02:58.645 --> 00:03:00.947 size:88% position:44% line:92%
you have had a bad idea.

00:03:00.947 --> 00:03:03.049 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I am not a cow.

00:03:03.049 --> 00:03:08.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm a fox.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:10.557 size:81% position:41% line:92%
-And I am not a bunny.

00:03:10.557 --> 00:03:13.927
I'm a whale.
Wait. I'm not good at this part.

00:03:13.927 --> 00:03:16.329 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I love you,
but that was not good.

00:03:16.329 --> 00:03:17.497 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:03:17.497 --> 00:03:19.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Look, we're glad that
you're fighting

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:20.667 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the ethical treatment
of animals.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:24.571 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Fight the good fight.
-Just don't drag us into this.

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:27.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪♪♪

